Hint: Apply the concept resultant of vectors.

Step:Find the correct match.
If two vectors are represented in magnitude and direction by two sides of a
triangle taken in order, then their resultant is represented in magnitude and
direction by the third side of the triangle taken in the opposite order.
In the first figure;

By applying triangle law of vector addition we get;
\(\overrightarrow {A}+ \overrightarrow {C} = \overrightarrow {B}\)
\(\Rightarrow \overrightarrow {B}-\overrightarrow {A}- \overrightarrow {C} =0\)
In the second figure;

By applying triangle law of vector addition we get;
\(\overrightarrow {A}+ \overrightarrow {B} +\overrightarrow {C}=0\)
\(\Rightarrow \overrightarrow {A}+ \overrightarrow {B} = -\overrightarrow {C}\)
In the third figure;

By applying triangle law of vector addition we get;
\(\overrightarrow {C}+ \overrightarrow {B} = \overrightarrow {A}\)
\(\Rightarrow \overrightarrow {A}-\overrightarrow {B}- \overrightarrow {C} =0\)
In the fourth figure;

By applying triangle law of vector addition we get;
\(\overrightarrow {A}+ \overrightarrow {B} = \overrightarrow {C}\)
\(\Rightarrow \overrightarrow {C}-\overrightarrow {B}- \overrightarrow {A} =0\)
Therefore, the correct match is\(\text { (a) } \rightarrow \text { (iv), (b) }
\rightarrow \text { (iii), (c) } \rightarrow \text { (i), (d) } \rightarrow
\text { (ii) }\).
